  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The partnership is pivoting from market-rate multifamily joint venture equity investments toward tax-exempt mortgage revenue bonds, a painful transition that is currently weighing on results. Legacy joint venture holdings are generating disproportionate losses, driving a drastic earnings miss and a collapse in investment income. Asset sale multiples have compressed, signaling a breakdown in the prior business model. Market sentiment has soured dramatically—units trade at a deep discount to book value after a steep decline, and institutional ownership has thinned, reflecting widespread skepticism about the near-term outlook.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has explicitly reiterated the repositioning plan, seeking to exit volatile market-rate equity exposures in favor of a more stable bond-focused structure. However, execution credibility has been severely damaged by the magnitude of the earnings miss and subsequent analyst downgrades. Targets were slashed sharply, and the market now awaits a clear guidance reset. While the partnership retains unrestricted cash, the abrupt strategy shift and guidance vacuum have eroded confidence; the overriding question is whether management can stabilize the business and restore trust before fundamentals deteriorate further.",
